DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppnnmmiinnddeexx  creates  an index image containing thumbnail (small) versions
       of a bunch of PNM files you supply.  (Akin to a  photographic  "contact
       sheet."

       ppnnmmiinnddeexx labels each thumbnail and, optionally, contains a title.

       If you just want to concatenate some images together in a grid, use ppaa‐‐
       mmuunnddiiccee for that.

       If you want to take apart the image you generated  with  ppnnmmiinnddeexx,  use
       ppaammddiiccee or ppaammccuutt.

       The  program  can generate large temporary files.  By default, these go
       in directory //ttmmpp, but you can usse the TTMMPPDDIIRR environment variable  to
       have them somewhere else.



OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In  addition  to  the options common to all programs based on libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ ), ppnnmmiinnddeexx  recognizes  the
       following command line options:



       --ssiizzee==_N
              The  size  of  each thumbnail.  The image is scaled to fit maxi‐
              mally inside a _N x _N pixel box without changing its  aspect  ra‐
              tio.  Default is 100.


       --aaccrroossss==_N
              The number of thumbnails in each row.  Default is 6.


       --ccoolloorrss==_N
              The  maximum  number of colors allowed in the overall image.  If
              it would otherwise have more colors than these,  ppnnmmiinnddeexx  quan‐
              tizes the result.  The default is 256.

              However,  this  value is meaningless if you specify the --nnooqquuaanntt
              option.


       --bbllaacckk This controls the color of the padding between the images;  nor‐
              mally  it's  white  and  the labels are black lettering on white
              background, but the --bbllaacckk option reverses this.


       --ttiittllee==_t_i_t_l_e
              Specifies a title top place at the top of the image.  Default is
              no title.


       --qquuaanntt Enables quantization (to the number of colors specified by --ccooll‐‐
              oorrss).  Quantization is on by default but you can disable it with
              --nnooqquuaanntt..


       --nnooqquuaanntt
              See --qquuaanntt.




